      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-237206",
      ":question/problem": "A particular feature is being examined across $3$ groups of individuals to determine if the mean varies by group. The summary statistics of three samples, one from each group, are given in the table below, where $n_{k}$ is the size of each sample, and $s_{k}$ is the sample standard deviation.\n\n|  | Sample 1 | Sample 2 | Sample 3 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $n_{k}$ | $15$ | $16$ | $31$ |\n| $s_{k}$ | $12.7$ | $13.6$ | $15.3$ |\n\nWhat is the sum of squares within groups (SSW) of these samples?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
